# Protections for the unbounded-scanf/strtoull variant corpus. Held IDENTICAL
# across every target in this family on purpose: the *shape of the unbounded
# write and of the leak* is the only variable, so a protection difference would
# confound the measurement. Every file in benchmark/corpus_scanf/ carries this
# same list, byte for byte, including the negative control.
#
# The set is the measured HTB target's set (auth-or-out: PIE, canary, Full
# RELRO, NX -- `checksec` measured 2026-09-27), because those four together are
# what makes this category hard: there is no fixed address to aim at until
# something has been leaked, and no writing past a canary until it is known.
#
# -fstack-protector-all  canary on EVERY function, so the canary is in the way
#                        of every frame the overflow could walk -- and, just as
#                        important, so gcc applies its stack-protector frame
#                        REORDERING (arrays hoisted above scalars). That
#                        reordering is why the reachable target of a %s overflow
#                        has to be a struct member rather than a sibling local,
#                        and the family is built around that fact.
# -pie -fPIE             PIE, as in the target: no code address is known until
#                        one is leaked, which is what the corpus's leak oracles
#                        are for.
# -Wl,-z,relro,-z,now    Full RELRO, as in the target: the GOT is read-only, so
#                        the usual "overwrite a GOT entry" shortcut is closed
#                        and the solve has to land on a return address or a
#                        live function pointer.
# -O0                    the whole category depends on the parsed scalar and the
#                        buffer living in addressable stack slots, and on the
#                        index/length being reloaded from memory at the point of
#                        use; at higher -O they live in registers, bounds get
#                        folded, and the target silently stops being in this
#                        category.
-fstack-protector-all
-pie
-fPIE
-Wl,-z,relro,-z,now
-O0
